      "side": 1,
      "message": "Two potential edge cases here:\n1. If PD_V_SINK_DISCONNECT_MAX \u003c vbus_mv \u003c PD_V_SAFE5V_MIN (3670..4750 mV), none of the branches match, leaving rv uninitialized and thresholds unconfigured. Consider using \u0027if (vbus_mv \u003e PD_V_SINK_DISCONNECT_MAX)\u0027 for the first branch.\n2. In the vbus_mv \u003c\u003d PD_V_SINK_DISCONNECT_MAX branch (line 591), SM5803_REG_VBUS_HIGH_TH is set to SM5803_VBUS_MAX_LEVEL (0xFF). If VBUS rises back to 5V before discharging below vSafe0V, the high-threshold interrupt won\u0027t fire. Consider setting HIGH_TH to SM5803_VBUS_PRESENT_LEVEL in this band as well.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "b3e65a92412bb020ed7fa5b7476fde2cdddb9176",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6e63b796_b7f54662",
