      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T17:48:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SM5803_REG_VBUS_LOW_TH compares the upper 8 bits of the 10-bit ADC (mv \u003d ((msb \u003c\u003c 2) | lsb) * 234 / 10). With 0x08 and 0x27, non-zero LSB bits (1..3) read back as 819 mV \u003e PD_V_SAFE0V_MAX (800 mV) and 3673..3720 mV \u003e PD_V_SINK_DISCONNECT_MAX (3670 mV), so sm5803_check_vbus_level() can still evaluate false when the low-threshold interrupt fires. Consider using 0x07 (\u003c\u003d 725 mV) and 0x26 (\u003c\u003d 3627 mV) so all LSB values satisfy the check.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "b3e65a92412bb020ed7fa5b7476fde2cdddb9176",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
